# Copy list

Reference: `src/app/(app)/cutting-orders/QtyCopyPopup.tsx` (opens from **Copy** on an order-products Fit List row).

When the user says **copy-list**, reuse this instead of a persisted table or the OS clipboard.

## What a copy is

A session snapshot of one product line’s **saved** size/drop qty cells, plus **item**, **size chart**, and the size/drop subset needed to draw the grid. Copies live in memory while the **order-details-panel** is open for that order. They are cleared when the panel closes or another order is opened. They are not saved across refresh.

## Chrome

- Popup over the order (portal). Title **Copy • {model}**. Escape / overlay / × close the popup (copies stay).
- Top of the list: **Copy** (samples the opening line; hide if that grid is empty) and **Clear** (empties the list).
- Fit List of copies: **item**, size/drop matrix, **total**, **Paste** + **Delete**.
- **Paste** only when the copy’s item and size chart match the opening line. Hide Paste otherwise.
- Empty target grid pastes immediately (replace). If the line is already sized: **This product is already sized** — **Replace**, **Combine** (same as scale-panel: add qtys; add missing size/drop to the product subset), **Cancel**. After a successful Paste, close the popup. Copies stay until the order panel closes.

## Customer orders

The customer-order products panel uses this same popup on a merchandise row. Freight and surcharge have no **Copy**. Paste writes size/drop quantities on `customer_order_cells` and leaves the line price, size extras, and `qty_shipped`. Replace refuses when a shipped quantity would be cleared. Copies clear when that order’s panel closes or another order is opened.
